  "notes": "ETYMOLOGY:\n{歌|か} (song, to sing) + {唱|しょう} (to chant, to recite). Both characters relate to vocal production.\n\nUSAGE:\nA formal term used in music criticism, competitions, and professional contexts. For casual singing (e.g., karaoke), {歌|うた}う is more natural. {歌唱|かしょう} emphasizes the technical and artistic aspect of singing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {歌唱力|かしょうりょく}: singing ability, vocal prowess\n- {歌唱|かしょう}を{披露|ひろう}する: to give a vocal performance\n- {歌唱|かしょう}{指導|しどう}: vocal coaching\n- {歌唱|かしょう}{技術|ぎじゅつ}: vocal technique\n- {歌唱|かしょう}する: to sing (formal)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {歌|うた}う: to sing (everyday, general)\n- {合唱|がっしょう}: chorus, singing in unison",
